{%- comment -%}
  Takes the theme's own price off the product page once the Bundlex offer widget has
  drawn itself.

  The widget prices every offer it shows, and the price block above it prices the bare
  variant, so the page carries two different numbers for the same purchase and only
  one of them is what the shopper will actually pay. The theme's is the one to go.

  It goes on sight of the widget rather than on page load, because the widget belongs
  to the app and does not always arrive: the app can be down, blocked by a shopper's
  extension, or simply switched off for a product. Nothing here happens until the
  widget is really on screen, so the worst case is the page the shopper used to get
  rather than one with no price on it at all.

  The widget is the app block Shopify renders inside the product information section,
  and this template has exactly one. If a second app block is ever added in there,
  narrow widget_selector to the widget's own wrapper or the price will disappear
  behind whatever else lands first.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign price_selector = '.product-information product-price'
  assign widget_selector = '.product-information .shopify-app-block, .product-information [id^="shopify-block-"]'
-%}

{%- if request.page_type == 'product' -%}
  <script
    type="application/json"
    id="voltairs-offer-price-config"
  >
    {
      "priceSelector": {{ price_selector | json }},
      "widgetSelector": {{ widget_selector | json }}
    }
  </script>
  <script src="{{ 'voltairs-offer-price.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
{%- endif -%}
